The Guidebook is a part of the game because it comes as
a part of the distribution.  There's no in-game way to
edit or display it, though.  As such, for folks who chose
using any in-game method of taking notes, the Guidebook.txt
may be a part of the game, but notepad.exe is no more a
part of the game than cmd.exe.  So there ;^)

The longer I play the less I care about most types of
notes.  Once I've IDed certain items, doing it the second
time in the same game is so much less a challenge it
hardly justifies taking notes on items.  If I'm playing a
wizard the Eye gives me transport to any branch, so there
is no point recording their levels.  If I'm playing a
Valk the Orb gives level teleport so all I need is the
one level of my main hoard or my short list of hoard
levels.  Currently I only record suspected luck number
and across saves I record whether it is safe to pray.


